    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ffe4bff_8af58065",
        "filename": "libc/syscalls.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 200,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-04T22:19:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e How about putting the recursive mutex logic into core/cortex-m/task.c\n\nPlease note that this implementation is compatible with architectures that provide atomic operations. I think we could put them in some common directory. On the other hand, I don\u0027t think this code will be used somewhere else. Zephyr mutexes are recursive, so I don\u0027t think we will reuse them.\n\nThat\u0027s why I decided to leave it here.",
      "parentUuid": "74e5346b_d612f9cf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 196,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 200,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "a5d4b76b41eba7d6e3671f4f338a2279fc35424c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08dae793_f56e7c80",
        "filename": "libc/syscalls.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 200,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-04T23:14:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e this implementation is compatible with architectures that provide atomic operations.\n\nOh, right.\n\nI don\u0027t love it, but we could surround the declarations in `task.h` for `mutex_lock_recursive`, etc. with `#if defined(CORTEX_M) \u0026\u0026 !defined(CONFIG_ZEPHYR)` and put the definition in `core/cortex-m/task.c`.\n\nI agree that we don\u0027t need it for Zephyr, but it seems *slightly* cleaner. (Or maybe it\u0027s just more consistent.)\n\nActually, as I\u0027m writing this I think I agree with you.\n\nWhat if we pull the recursive mutex code into a new file in the `libc` directory (e.g., `recursive_mutex.c` and `recursive_mutex.h`)? Then we could still use similar API names that we use in EC (e.g., `mutex_lock_recursive`, `mutex_unlock_recursive`, etc.), call those from this file, and write a unit test for those APIs. That would also avoid exposing the recursive mutex API to boards that don\u0027t use `libc`.",
      "parentUuid": "7ffe4bff_8af58065",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 196,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 200,
        "endChar": 2
      },
